From 682f37dfa6f4bc132d68bd944d903b527c5b2018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] CUDA: GP100: batched decode (several sequences, one
 token each) on the fp16 and fused state paths

Concurrent agents (llama-server --parallel N) decode one token for each of N
sequences per step. On GP100 most of the batch-1 work from 0007-0009 declined
that shape and fell back to stock kernels. This extends it (sm_60 only):

- MMVQ takes [K, 1, n_seqs] activations (qwen35's ssm_out) as n columns;
  they went to the emulated-int8 kernel at one column per sequence.
- Q6_K uses its multi-column kernel for 2..4 columns, with its activation
  reads made unconditional so the compiler shares them across rows
  (104 -> 60 loads per iteration); Q4_K/Q5_K multi-column epilogue is
  2 FMUL + 4 FFMA per (row, column).
- gated_delta_net reads the recurrent states of all sequences in place: one
  block covers a head's columns in every sequence and barriers between the
  state loads and stores, so a cell reordered by the recurrent memory (a
  source row that is another sequence's destination) is still read first.
  The q/k l2_norm and beta sigmoid fusions follow it.
- ssm_conv reads/writes the cached windows of every sequence in place (one
  thread per channel across all sequences, loads before stores).
- The fused RMS_NORM*weight+activation prep takes up to 8 rows when a matmul
  reads the result.
- Flash attention (on top of 0010): 2..4-token batches over a KV cache
  shorter than 65536 take the 2-head tile ladder instead of the 6-head fold,
  which is slower there (4 sequences: ~1.5k KV 82.9 vs 86.4 tok/s, 32k 74.3
  vs 76.0; at 98k the fold wins, 61.9 vs 60.5, and keeps it). One token,
  MTP-sized batches, prefill and q4_0 caches are unchanged.
- Every in-place state read now also proves that the recurrent memory's
  "extra" state copy (llm_graph_context::build_rs), which writes the same
  cache after the gather, is empty; otherwise the stock gather runs. This
  also covers the one-sequence paths from 0009.

2x P100, -sm tensor, Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, llama-batched-bench decode
(tok/s aggregate): 1 seq 35.2 -> 35.7, 2 seqs 48.6 -> 59.0, 4 seqs 68.0 ->
86.9, 8 seqs 83.8 -> 98.4. State fusions are bit-identical to the stock
kernels at 4 sequences; one-sequence output is unchanged in every digit.

